    "reasoning": "All 16 final answers agree with their own captured Math Academy solutions, but three solutions contain intermediate source errors. q-54476 incorrectly prints the upper limit of 4x as -1 rather than 1; its areas 11 and 8 and total 19 are correct. q-49024 incorrectly evaluates f'(e^2) as -1/(e^2 ln(10)); the correct value is -1/(e^4 ln(10)), still negative. q-49032 incorrectly labels its first table interval (-infinity,0) rather than (-2,0). These errors do not change the selected answers, so all disagrees flags are false. Independently: q-78868 has center (-4,7). q-10045 integrates to ln(1+sin(x)), giving the stated endpoint difference. q-84716 has y^2=-4x, generated by x=-t^2,y=-2t. q-106421 has y^2=16x, generated by x=4t^2,y=8t. q-54476 splits absolute area at x=-1, yielding 11+8=19. q-54494 splits at x=1, yielding 4/5+26/5=6. q-49622 substitutes u=8x+1, yielding (3sqrt(3)-1)/12. q-113750 has f'=-6(x-2)(2x+1), changing from positive to negative at x=2. q-49024 has derivative (1-ln(x))/(x^2 ln(10)), changing from positive to negative at e. q-21496 has derivative 3x^2-48/x^2, changing from negative to positive at 2. q-113766 has derivative 11x^10, positive on both sides of its sole stationary point, so no local extrema. q-49032 has derivative x^2(x+3)/(x+2)^2, positive throughout its domain except at zero, so no local extrema. q-20909 has speed sqrt(1/4+e^(2t)), equivalent to the selected integral. q-81708 integrates acceleration to 4/(2+t)+C, and v(0)=2 gives C=0. q-3293 has average 9+4c-c^2=-3, whose positive solution is 6. q-109275 has velocity 2(t-3)/((t-3)^2+1), zero only at t=3. No submitted grade or earlier answer is provided; confirmation of MA's final answers rests on the captured worked solutions.",
